Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:00:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] winemac.drv: Quit with Command-Q when Command is Ctrl.

With LeftCommandIsCtrl or RightCommandIsCtrl, Command-Q reached the
program as Ctrl-Q, which most Windows programs ignore, so the Mac's
Quit shortcut did nothing; Quit stayed on Option-Command-Q. Command-Q
now quits, as in every Mac app, and the program is still asked to
close (it can offer to save). Without the option nothing changes, so
Command-Q stays free for the program's Alt-Q.

Tried with Enterprise Architect under Gentes: Command-Q closes it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
index 0f4034b883..4615b9b7d2 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
@@ -270,7 +270,13 @@ - (void) transformProcessToForeground:(BOOL)activateIfTransformed
             else
                 title = WineLocalizedString(STRING_MENU_ITEM_QUIT);
             item = [submenu addItemWithTitle:title action:@selector(terminate:) keyEquivalent:@"q"];
-            [item setKeyEquivalentModifierMask:NSEventModifierFlagCommand | NSEventModifierFlagOption];
+            /* With Command as Ctrl, Command-Q quits as in every Mac app instead of reaching the
+               program as Ctrl-Q, which most Windows programs ignore; otherwise it stays free for
+               the program's Alt-Q. */
+            if (left_command_is_ctrl || right_command_is_ctrl)
+                [item setKeyEquivalentModifierMask:NSEventModifierFlagCommand];
+            else
+                [item setKeyEquivalentModifierMask:NSEventModifierFlagCommand | NSEventModifierFlagOption];
             item = [[[NSMenuItem alloc] init] autorelease];
             [item setTitle:WineLocalizedString(STRING_MENU_WINE)];
             [item setSubmenu:submenu];
